IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- coa9-laying.l4: Companies Act 2006 (UK), Part 15 Chapter 8: public companies, laying of accounts and reports before general meeting
-- (ss 437, 438), lines 5842-5851 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa9-strategic.l4. A defence is answered as ruling (b) of 2026-11-05 says: JUST TRUE where the facts
-- prove it, JUST FALSE worded "this section gives no defence on these facts" (never "no defence at all") where they do not.
--
-- REGULATIVE RULE. Section 437(1) and (2) is also written as a regulative rule, `s 437 the directors of a public company must lay copies
-- before the company in general meeting`, run with #TRACE in coa9-tests-laying.l4; its twin decision function `s 437(2) the directors laid
-- the copies in time` is asserted, because a #TRACE adds no assertion line to the counts check.sh prints.
--
-- s 438(4) carries two versions of its daily default fine in this text (see the fork register, F30, and NEEDS-CORE.md).

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 437: Public companies: laying of accounts and reports before general meeting
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `s 437 Public companies: laying of accounts and reports before general meeting`

-- src:5843 | 437 Public companies: laying of accounts and reports before general meeting
-- src:5844 | (1) The directors of a public company must lay before the company in general meeting copies of its annual accounts and reports.
@ref s 437(1) The directors of a public company must lay copies of the annual accounts and reports before the company in general meeting (src:5843-5844)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have laid before the company in general meeting copies of its annual accounts and reports` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 437(1) the directors of the public company have laid copies of the annual accounts and reports before the company in general meeting` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 4(2) the company is a public company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The directors of a public company"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
    ELSE IF `the directors have laid before the company in general meeting copies of its annual accounts and reports`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F31): "The directors of a public company must lay before the company in general meeting copies of its annual accounts and reports."

-- src:5845 | (2) This section must be complied with not later than the end of the period for filing the accounts and reports in question.
@ref s 437(2) The laying must be done not later than the end of the period for filing (src:5845)
GIVEN `the day the copies were laid before the company in general meeting` IS A DATE
      `s 442 the end of the period for filing accounts and reports` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 437(2) the directors laid the copies in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the copies were laid before the company in general meeting` AT MOST `s 442 the end of the period for filing accounts and reports`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a period fixed in the text's own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "This section must be complied with not later than the end of the period for filing the accounts and reports in question."

-- Section 437(1) and (2) as a regulative rule. The clock counts days from `the day the obligation arises`; the last day is the end of the
-- period for filing (inclusive).
@ref s 437(2) The laying must be done not later than the end of the period for filing (src:5845)
DECLARE `s 437 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 437 lay copies of the annual accounts and reports before the company in general meeting`

-- src:5843 | 437 Public companies: laying of accounts and reports before general meeting
-- src:5844 | (1) The directors of a public company must lay before the company in general meeting copies of its annual accounts and reports.
-- src:5845 | (2) This section must be complied with not later than the end of the period for filing the accounts and reports in question.
@ref s 437(1), (2) The directors of a public company must lay the accounts and reports before the company in general meeting not later than the end of the period for filing (src:5843-5845)
GIVEN `the day the obligation arises` IS A DATE
      `s 442 the end of the period for filing accounts and reports` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 437 action`
`s 437 the directors of a public company must lay copies before the company in general meeting` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `s 437 lay copies of the annual accounts and reports before the company in general meeting`
    WITHIN (Day `s 442 the end of the period for filing accounts and reports` MINUS Day `the day the obligation arises`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "copies of the annual accounts and reports were not laid before the company in general meeting by the end of the period for filing"

-- src:5846 | (3) In the Companies Acts“accounts meeting”, in relation to a public company, means a general meeting of the company at which the company's annual accounts and reports are (or are to be) laid in accordance with this section.
@ref s 437(3) Meaning of "accounts meeting" in relation to a public company (src:5846)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is a general meeting of the company at which the company's annual accounts and reports are (or are to be) laid in accordance with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 437(3) the meeting is an accounts meeting` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 4(2) the company is a public company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "“accounts meeting”, in relation to a public company"
    ELSE IF `the meeting is a general meeting of the company at which the company's annual accounts and reports are (or are to be) laid in accordance with this section`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“accounts meeting”, in relation to a public company, means a general meeting of the company at which the company's annual accounts and reports are (or are to be) laid in accordance with this section"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 438: Public companies: offence of failure to lay accounts and reports
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `s 438 Public companies: offence of failure to lay accounts and reports`

-- src:5847 | 438 Public companies: offence of failure to lay accounts and reports
-- src:5848 | (1) If the requirements of section 437 (public companies: laying of accounts and reports before general meeting) are not complied with before the end of the period allowed, every person who immediately before the end of that period was a director of the company commits an offence.
@ref s 438(1) Every person who was a director immediately before the end of the period allowed commits an offence if section 437 was not complied with (src:5847-5848)
GIVEN `the requirements of section 437 were not complied with before the end of the period allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a director of the company immediately before the end of that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 438(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the requirements of section 437 were not complied with before the end of the period allowed`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer): "If the requirements of section 437 ... are not complied with before the end of the period allowed, every person who immediately before the end of that period was a director of the company commits an offence"
    ELSE IF `the person was a director of the company immediately before the end of that period`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every person who immediately before the end of that period was a director of the company"

-- src:5849 | (2) It is a defence for a person charged with such an offence to prove that he took all reasonable steps for securing that those requirements would be complied with before the end of that period.
@ref s 438(2) A defence: all reasonable steps were taken (src:5849)
GIVEN `the person is charged with an offence under section 438` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves that he took all reasonable steps for securing that those requirements would be complied with before the end of that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 438(2) this section gives the person a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person is charged with an offence under section 438`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person charged with such an offence"
    ELSE IF `the person proves that he took all reasonable steps for securing that those requirements would be complied with before the end of that period`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a defence the facts do not prove, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); "this section gives no defence on these facts", not "no defence at all"): "It is a defence for a person charged with such an offence to prove that he took all reasonable steps for securing that those requirements would be complied with before the end of that period"

-- src:5850 | (3) It is not a defence to prove that the documents in question were not in fact prepared as required by this Part.
@ref s 438(3) It is not a defence to prove that the documents were not in fact prepared (src:5850)
GIVEN `the person proves that the documents in question were not in fact prepared as required by this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 438(3) proof that the documents were not in fact prepared as required is a defence` MEANS
    IF `the person proves that the documents in question were not in fact prepared as required by this Part`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is not a defence to prove that the documents in question were not in fact prepared as required by this Part."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of proof that the documents were not prepared

-- s 438(4): the penalty. The text as rendered reads "... a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater
-- of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale." It carries two versions of the daily default fine, run together, and does not say which is in force (fork F30).
-- The core has a constructor for "one-tenth of level 5" (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1) and none for the greater of an amount and a level
-- (recorded in NEEDS-CORE.md); this module declares the second under its own prefix.
@ref s 438(3) It is not a defence to prove that the documents were not in fact prepared (src:5850)
DECLARE `s 438(4) version of the daily default fine` IS ONE OF
    `s 438(4) the first version: one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale`
    `s 438(4) the second version: one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale`

-- src:5851 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 438(4) Penalty for an offence under section 438: level 5 and a daily default fine in one of two versions (src:5851)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 438(4) the penalty for an offence under section 438` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1), NOTHING, FALSE) -- NOTHING-kind (silent) for the daily default fine: the text carries two versions and does not say which is in force, fork F30
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection provides only for liability on summary conviction

@ref s 438(4) (src:5851)
GIVEN version IS A `s 438(4) version of the daily default fine`
      `the pounds level 4 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
      `the pounds level 5 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 438(4) the most the daily default fine may be in pounds on the version` MEANS
    CONSIDER version
    WHEN `s 438(4) the first version: one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale` THEN `the pounds level 5 on the standard scale stands for` DIVIDED BY 10
    WHEN `s 438(4) the second version: one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale` THEN
        (max 5000 `the pounds level 4 on the standard scale stands for`) DIVIDED BY 10
